#: ../../source/docs/code-overview-adding-support-for-a-new-mavlink-gimbal.rst:5
#: 380bac1f29324f4398f8560982980047
msgid "Adding Support for a new MAVLink Gimbal"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/code-overview-adding-support-for-a-new-mavlink-gimbal.rst:7
#: 9554b5ee164247c380f41f5c2e76efa4
msgid "This page covers how ArduPilot interacts with a MAVLink enabled gimbal. It is meant more as a guide on how gimbal manufacturers can make their gimbals work with ArduPilot with minimum code changes to ArduPilot ."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/code-overview-adding-support-for-a-new-mavlink-gimbal.rst:11
#: c4b3fd6e96004ce88ba51c65aa891d94
msgid "The :ref:`SToRM32 gimbal <copter:common-storm32-gimbal>` is a good reference as it supports MAVLink."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/code-overview-adding-support-for-a-new-mavlink-gimbal.rst:15
#: e4f95548f1a84ca68457231ccd9bf075
msgid "Messages the gimbal should support"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/code-overview-adding-support-for-a-new-mavlink-gimbal.rst:17
#: 634953950511484db2d51c7f7c928d63
msgid "The gimbal should listen on the serial port for a `HEARTBEAT <https://mavlink.io/en/messages/common.html#HEARTBEAT>`__ message from the vehicle. It can generally assume that the first heart beat it receives will be from the vehicle but to be certain you can check the \"type\" field to be sure it's something sensible (i.e. MAV_TYPE = 1 for fixed wing, 2 for quadcopters but 6 for GCSs should be ignored)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/code-overview-adding-support-for-a-new-mavlink-gimbal.rst:25
#: c095d975a74141a09fe0c52673bde50c
msgid "This heart beat will contain the vehicle's system-id and component-id.  The gimbal should adopt the same system-id but should use a component-id of MAV_COMP_ID_GIMBAL (i.e. 154) for all its future messages.  In fact, any unique component-id can be used as long as it's not zero nor the component id of the vehicle or any other device on the vehicle."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/code-overview-adding-support-for-a-new-mavlink-gimbal.rst:31
#: 84c8ea343c72481492b57841f79cd3a9
msgid "The gimbal should send a `HEARTBEAT <https://mavlink.io/en/messages/common.html#HEARTBEAT>`__ message out the serial port at approximately 1hz"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/code-overview-adding-support-for-a-new-mavlink-gimbal.rst:35
#: 6380ffedb3ca4fbfb300ff6bf50f89ad
msgid "the system-id and component-id should be as mentioned above."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/code-overview-adding-support-for-a-new-mavlink-gimbal.rst:36
#: 44bbf9056daf409cb194e6fb66c54f2e
msgid "\"type\" should be MAV_TYPE_GIMBAL (i.e. 26)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/code-overview-adding-support-for-a-new-mavlink-gimbal.rst:37
#: 9cd7934f95e24da1b6b16de7fa829d5c
msgid "\"autopilot\" is not used so can be set to anything including MAV_AUTOPILOT_GENERIC (i.e. 0)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/code-overview-adding-support-for-a-new-mavlink-gimbal.rst:39
#: ae67f1f50964423fb625d64f53d25931
msgid "\"base_mode\" and \"custom_mode\" are not used so can be set to anything (perhaps 0 is best)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/code-overview-adding-support-for-a-new-mavlink-gimbal.rst:41
#: 05f636d16b0341898fbd2ffcf1c0530e
msgid "\"system_status\" should be set to \"MAV_STATE_ACTIVE\" once the gimbal is ready to accept attitude targets"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/code-overview-adding-support-for-a-new-mavlink-gimbal.rst:44
#: 891496c183db44f7aac13c7620f57cab
msgid "To support reading/writing parameter values from the ground station the gimbal should implement these message:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/code-overview-adding-support-for-a-new-mavlink-gimbal.rst:47
#: a3af356d832442379df130b8570c0a4f
msgid "`PARAM_REQUEST_READ <https://mavlink.io/en/messages/common.html#PARAM_REQUEST_READ>`__ - if the gimbal receives this message and \"target_system\" and \"target_component\" values match the gimbal's system-id and component-id, it should respond with a `PARAM_VALUE <https://mavlink.io/en/messages/common.html#PARAM_VALUE>`__ message which contains the value of the parameter specified by the \"param_id\" field (simply an enum, the gimbal can assign whatever enum it wishes to each of its internal parameters)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/code-overview-adding-support-for-a-new-mavlink-gimbal.rst:55
#: e3f5f31d0a62440f9a038eac604ae82d
msgid "`PARAM_REQUEST_LIST <https://mavlink.io/en/messages/common.html#PARAM_REQUEST_LIST>`__ - respond to this message by sending a `PARAM_VALUE <https://mavlink.io/en/messages/common.html#PARAM_VALUE>`__ message for every parameter within the gimbal."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/code-overview-adding-support-for-a-new-mavlink-gimbal.rst:59
#: 5c5ddc789f1c4add8e00a7ce84d3be0a
msgid "`PARAM_SET <https://mavlink.io/en/messages/common.html#PARAM_SET>`__ - respond to this by setting the internal variable to the value in the \"param_value\" field."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/code-overview-adding-support-for-a-new-mavlink-gimbal.rst:63
#: f2a21bb1652345dfa42ffc64a571269c
msgid "ArduPilot will send angle requests to the gimbal via MAVLink which will arrive as `COMMAND_LONG <https://mavlink.io/en/messages/common.html#COMMAND_LONG>`__ messages with the \"command\" field set to MAV_CMD_DO_MOUNT_CONTROL (i.e 205)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/code-overview-adding-support-for-a-new-mavlink-gimbal.rst:69
#: cf6d6e51b5b442bf9fb6a0f1c7de0d00
msgid "Param #1 contains desired pitch in degrees"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/code-overview-adding-support-for-a-new-mavlink-gimbal.rst:70
#: 9f609aff9c7143c1973b6fef22d13f88
msgid "Param #2 contains desired roll in degrees"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/code-overview-adding-support-for-a-new-mavlink-gimbal.rst:71
#: a5b0debe4168461db589e8e1ce035392
msgid "Param #3 contains desired yaw in degrees but note that the yaw is in relation to the front of the vehicle so \"0\" is straight ahead, \"90\" is to the right, \"-90\" is to the left."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/code-overview-adding-support-for-a-new-mavlink-gimbal.rst:75
#: cea5c9cf7458480caefcf25a27b1c845
msgid "If the gimbal needs extra data from the vehicle it can request it using the `REQUEST_DATA_STREAM <https://mavlink.io/en/messages/common.html#REQUEST_DATA_STREAM>`__ message."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/code-overview-adding-support-for-a-new-mavlink-gimbal.rst:80
#: b173382c0ed344f29342a2362ad3dda3
msgid "the target system and component id should be for the vehicle."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/code-overview-adding-support-for-a-new-mavlink-gimbal.rst:81
#: f58eebc278e64c9cae65e5d352c7de55
msgid "\"req_stream_id\" can be any values in the MAV_DATA_STREAM enum. Some useful values are:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/code-overview-adding-support-for-a-new-mavlink-gimbal.rst:84
#: 2846cebe4332418eb792be2e3eb34d50
msgid "MAV_DATA_STREAM_POSITION will cause the vehicle to send `GLOBAL_POSITION_INT <https://mavlink.io/en/messages/common.html#GLOBAL_POSITION_INT>`__ messages which includes lat, lon, alt, velocity (3d) and heading)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/code-overview-adding-support-for-a-new-mavlink-gimbal.rst:88
#: 8b1a9f9da2e242a582367f1be5419973
msgid "MAV_DATA_STREAM_EXTRA1 will send the `MSG_ATTITUDE <https://mavlink.io/en/messages/common.html#ATTITUDE>`__ which includes euler angles for roll, pitch, yaw"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/code-overview-adding-support-for-a-new-mavlink-gimbal.rst:93
#: 314ae6bbe0744cc7aa4f19d4dd6ba1b0
msgid "Testing"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/code-overview-adding-support-for-a-new-mavlink-gimbal.rst:95
#: 8fd3e2262f524e6b8fd1867dfe552452
msgid "To test the system, you should be able to connect the gimbal to a Pixhawk as if it's a SToRM32 gimbal. In particular check the `\"Set-up through the Mission Planner (MALVink protocol)\" <http://copter.ardupilot.com/wiki/common-storm32-gimbal/#set-up_through_the_mission_planner_mavlink_protocol>`__ section."
msgstr ""
